    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a balanced slate today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker**, who commands our highest efficiency score of 73.479. Facing Tyler Phillips, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable 4.52 xERA matchup and a positive dynamic platoon adjustment, cementing his status as the primary offensive anchor. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.701) also presents a strong profile against Kyle Bradish; while the platoon adjustment is slightly negative, the elite SP skill correlation and a favorable park factor keep him as a must-start staple in the #3 hole. **Heliot Ramos** (57.608) and **Gunnar Henderson** (58.622) round out the high-ceiling group, with **Gunnar Henderson** particularly noteworthy for overcoming a tough 3.20 xERA matchup through a massive +14% platoon advantage.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with **Jackson Merrill** (46.037) and **Wade Meckler** (41.418). **Jackson Merrill** is a classic \"gamble\" play today\u2014while his base projection took a hit from a brutal matchup against Cesar Perdomo, the +10% wind-out factor kept him marginally relevant. Our toughest decision was at the bench, where **Coby Mayo** (38.122) narrowly missed the cut. Despite decent power potential, the optimizer pushed **Coby Mayo** out in favor of safer utility options, penalized heavily by the -19% SP skill friction against Spencer Miles.\n\nRisk management remains critical as several starters remain pending official confirmation. We are operating under the assumption that **Drake Baldwin** (59.112) hits leadoff, as his high floor makes him an ideal table-setter regardless of the lack of opposing SP data. We are also monitoring **Nasim Nunez**, whose score of 54.896 is hampered by an elite defensive catcher behind the plate, limiting his upside as a stolen base threat. With **Andy Pages**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** all sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, necessitating a disciplined approach to avoid wasting game caps on suboptimal matchups. We continue to monitor the status of **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tommy White** for potential rotation shifts should the final lineups deviate significantly from our projections.",
